# AVP Game Hub — your machine's settings. Copy to local/config.env (gitignored) and fill in.
# Read by klepton/build_run_vpro.sh, klepton/visionos/run.sh, klepton/visionos/stage_alyx.sh,
# klepton/visionos/gen_xcodeproj.py and the Mac app. Anything set in the environment wins.

# Your Apple Developer team id (10 characters). Optional: detected from the login keychain's
# "Apple Development" certificate (created when you sign in under Xcode › Settings › Accounts).
KLEPTON_TEAM=

# Your Vision Pro's UDID (`xcrun devicectl list devices`). Optional: the first paired
# physical Vision Pro is used when unset.
KLEPTON_DEVICE=

# The hub's bundle id. REQUIRED for device builds, and yours to choose: an App ID your team can
# register, under your own reverse domain, e.g. com.<you>.avpgamehub (com.example.* and
# com.yourname.* are refused). Keep it once you have installed: game data lives in its container.
KLEPTON_BUNDLE_ID=

# Optional: build only some games, e.g. KLEPTON_HUB_GAMES=superhot,ktane ("none" = library only).
# Unset = every game whose files are on this Mac (docs/GUIDE.md, "Getting each game's files").
#KLEPTON_HUB_GAMES=

# Optional: 1 attaches the com.apple.developer.low-latency-streaming entitlement. Off by default:
# it is not self-service, and a team that was never granted it fails signing.
#KLEPTON_LOW_LATENCY=1

# Optional: 1 gives the hub iCloud Drive (container iCloud.<KLEPTON_BUNDLE_ID>) for the iCloud
# backups of the Meta games' saves. Off by default: the App ID needs the iCloud capability with
# that container (automatic signing adds it on a device build). Off, the hub says "iCloud not
# available" in each game's settings and backs nothing up.
#KLEPTON_ICLOUD=1
